+# Request 14 archive copy: visible production-label census
+
+**TEL01.** This follows the [acquired 28-page archive copy](../telephone-doj-request14-member-2026-11-15/README.md), SHA-256 `957eecd527e1f1ee56867704b630c81edb766e76b8519b95abb5e660ac335f20`, retrieved 2026-11-15 from the [2009 Commission-records ZIP mirror](https://archive.org/download/911datasets/NARA_9-11_Commission_Records_Released_Jan_14_2009.zip). The source's exact member path and range are pinned in that report.
+
+**Observed in the acquired PDF.** The right-footer review of every physical page identified these sequential M-WFA production-label suffixes:
+
+| Physical PDF pages | Visible suffixes | Count |
+| --- | --- | ---: |
+| 2–10 | 600–608, in order | 9 |
+| 11–24 | 632–645, in order | 14 |
+
+The right-footer crops for p. 1 and pp. 25–28 did not show a production label in that crop; that limited observation is not a whole-page absence finding. The cover separately describes 50 enclosed pages. The numerical label gap **609–631** comprises 23 labels; it does not by itself establish 23 missing physical pages, identify their content, or explain the source copy's assembly. The earlier separate hosted-reader review described the same label gap. No image-equivalence comparison with that reader, native delivery or full release was made. [Prior source review](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/74b2133ec389d68dd9906ccf89894442d07b58b7/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-landscape-review-2026-10-27/README.md)
+
+**Method and limits.** Rendered all 28 pages at 100 dpi and inspected a contact sheet of cropped right footers. OCR assisted identification but made errors on three labels; visual reading of the cropped labels, rather than uncorrected OCR, supports the ranges above. This is a label inventory, not a review of every page body, independent delivery authentication, call count, duration or device test. The original PDF and working images contain sensitive fields and remain outside this public derivative.
